{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1864","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"H. Asterism Stream"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bogocubic is playing a game with amenotiomoi. First, Bogocubic fixed an integer $$$n$$$, and then he gave amenotiomoi an integer $$$x$$$ which is initially equal to $$$1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one move amenotiomoi performs "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the following operations with the same probability:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" increase $$$x$$$ by $$$1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" multiply $$$x$$$ by $$$2$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bogocubic wants to find the expected number of moves amenotiomoi has to do to make $$$x$$$ greater than or equal to $$$n$$$. Help him find this number modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Formally, let $$$M = 998\\,244\\,353$$$. It can be shown that the answer can be expressed as an irreducible fraction $$$\\frac{p}{q}$$$, where $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$ are integers and $$$q \\not \\equiv 0 \\pmod{M}$$$. Output the integer equal to $$$p \\cdot q^{-1} \\bmod M$$$. In other words, output such an integer $$$y$$$ that $$$0 \\le y \\lt M$$$ and $$$y \\cdot q \\equiv p \\pmod{M}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 100$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^{18}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the expected number of moves modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n1\n4\n8\n15\n998244353\n296574916252563317\n494288321850420024\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n499122179\n717488133\n900515847\n93715054\n44488799\n520723508\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, $$$n\\le x$$$ without any operations, so the answer is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, for $$$n = 4$$$, here is the list of all possible sequences of operations and their probabilities:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1\\stackrel{+1}{\\longrightarrow}2\\stackrel{+1}{\\longrightarrow}3\\stackrel{+1}{\\longrightarrow}4$$$, the probability is $$$\\frac{1}{8}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1\\stackrel{\\times 2}{\\longrightarrow}2\\stackrel{+1}{\\longrightarrow}3\\stackrel{+1}{\\longrightarrow}4$$$, the probability is $$$\\frac{1}{8}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1\\stackrel{+1}{\\longrightarrow}2\\stackrel{+1}{\\longrightarrow}3\\stackrel{\\times 2}{\\longrightarrow}6$$$, the probability is $$$\\frac{1}{8}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1\\stackrel{\\times 2}{\\longrightarrow}2\\stackrel{+1}{\\longrightarrow}3\\stackrel{\\times 2}{\\longrightarrow}6$$$, the probability is $$$\\frac{1}{8}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1\\stackrel{+1}{\\longrightarrow}2\\stackrel{\\times 2}{\\longrightarrow}4$$$, the probability is $$$\\frac{1}{4}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1\\stackrel{\\times 2}{\\longrightarrow}2\\stackrel{\\times 2}{\\longrightarrow}4$$$, the probability is $$$\\frac{1}{4}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So the expected number of moves is $$$4 \\cdot \\left(3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8}\\right) + 2 \\cdot \\left(2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\right) =\\frac{5}{2} \\equiv 499122179 \\pmod{998244353}$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, for $$$n = 8$$$, the expected number of moves is $$$\\frac{137}{32}\\equiv 717488133\\pmod{998244353}$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth test case, for $$$n = 15$$$, the expected number of moves is $$$\\frac{24977}{4096} \\equiv 900515847 \\pmod{998244353}$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"H","problemCode":"1864H","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1864/problem/H"}